-----------
 macnotify
-----------

Run a command when macOS appearance changes, after wake, and once at startup.

```sh
cargo install --path . --root ~/.local
macnotify /path/to/command arg1 arg2
macnotify /bin/bash /path/to/script.sh
macnotify --retry 5,15 /path/to/command
```

Commands run one at a time, with no retries by default. `--retry 5,15` retries
twice: 5 seconds after failure, then 15 seconds after the next failure. A new
event starts a fresh attempt. Commands should read the current state and return.
Arguments are passed unchanged; no event name or appearance value is added.

To run at login, copy `examples/macnotify.plist` to
`~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.macnotify.plist`. Set the absolute paths to
macnotify and your command, then load it:

```sh
launchctl bootstrap "gui/$(id -u)" ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.macnotify.plist
```

Stop it with `launchctl bootout "gui/$(id -u)/local.macnotify"`.

AI Training
-----------

Do not use this project's code, documentation, or other materials to train
or fine-tune AI/ML models, including large language models, or include them
in training datasets. The author expressly objects to those uses and asks
dataset maintainers and model developers to exclude these materials unless
the author has separately agreed in writing.

This declaration states the author's wishes.
